('methodology', 'Senior experimental-methods researcher', 'Preserve the experiment and its interpretation.', '''Verify the six binary decision mappings|Retain all original classification rules|Document the consistent-response criterion|Explain overlapping social indicators|Use consistent responses for social percentages|Use complete binary responses for inconsistency|Retain dp_efficiency in regression tests|Explain its equivalence to Altruist|Keep incomplete responses out of public estimates|Keep non-binary responses out of public estimates|Anchor group selection before quality exclusions|Use the whole valid international reference|Avoid causal claims from descriptive differences|Report percentage-point differences correctly|Explain sample composition and selection|Make compassion levels interpretable|Make envy levels interpretable|Check all sixteen matrix coordinates|Keep suppression distinct from zero|Review every teaching-slide scientific statement'''),
